=== Strategy ===
The Ant Queen has around 900 HP and can deal very fair damage, in the 100's if you allow your openings to get high, by using her access to powerful moves like Blood & Gore and Bear Down, and her Chomp is nothing to scoff at either.

Unfortunately for her however, she is pathetically slow (33.33 U/s movespeed) and can be easily outrun by any Hearthling on Run (~50 U/s movespeed). Due to this, and the fact she has no armor, she can easily be killed through one of two methods:

* Easy, quick method: Just kite her in circles. Aggro only her and not her minions, and bring her to an empty room. (The reason you do this is because her minions can respawn in her arena, but nowhere else.) If her minions aggro, bring them too and pick them off one by one until it's just you and her. Alternatively if you have allies, have one person distract the minions while the rest draw her away. Then just run in circles tapping her with attacks and always keep your openings low. Eventually she will go down. That is to say unless you simply stand and deliver on her, which can be comfortably done around 90 UA/MC and 60 AGI. Then she can be killed in mere moments with well timed and well opened cleaves or full circles.
* Easier, slower method: Use this method if you're far underlevelled and made it here through dumb luck and determination or assaulting her hill with sheer numbers. Do just as with method 1, bringing her away from her arena and isolating her from her minions. Then just kite her in circles and sling rocks or shoot arrows at her; there is nothing she can do about it and she won't even bother fleeing from you. 

'''WARNING! Upon killing her, the dungeon will begin shaking and you will have EXACTLY 5 MINUTES to pack up and escape!''' If those 5 minutes elapse, all Hearthlings will be harmlessly booted out of the dungeon and it will destroy itself. Why is that a problem? Because ''only Hearthlings are booted out.'' Anything else in the dungeon, any loot, the Queen or her minion's corpses, the Small Heart Container, any objects you built or brought into the dungeon, even ''tamed animals like your horse'' will be instantly deleted once all Hearthlings are booted and the hill collapses. Do not test the timer! Grab the heart container, the queen's corpse, and any horses you might have brought, and leave. Any looting or butchering of other parts of the dungeon should be done before killing the queen.

